non-destructive testing before the

129
00:08:55,487 --> 00:08:57,784
component is cleared for deployment.

130
00:08:57,784 --> 00:09:02,145
As you evaluate visual depictions of
additive metal production, pay close

131
00:09:02,145 --> 00:09:06,745
attention to how manufacturing systems
balance extreme thermal energy against

132
00:09:06,745 --> 00:09:09,971
physical material limits across research
institutions.

133
00:09:09,971 --> 00:09:14,491
High-speed melt pool keyhole imaging
captured by NIST demonstrates that metal

134
00:09:14,491 --> 00:09:19,188
3D printing is not merely depositing hot
material like plastic filament; it is a

135
00:09:19,188 --> 00:09:23,943
rapid phase transformation governed by
high cooling rate dynamics measured by the

136
00:09:23,943 --> 00:09:25,176
Fraunhofer Institute.

137
00:09:25,176 --> 00:09:30,105
When observing high-magnification
micrographs of printed alloys, notice how

138
00:09:30,105 --> 00:09:35,428
microstructural grain size data documented
by ASM International clarifies why raw

139
00:09:35,428 --> 00:09:38,451
